1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:00,442
Hi!

2
00:00:00,442 --> 00:00:02,137
Meet Qb and Qbo, my two cats.

3
00:00:02,137 --> 00:00:04,074
They look so alike that my camera can't

4
00:00:04,074 --> 00:00:04,800
tell them apart.

5
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,200
I'm at work all day.

6
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,200
I just want to know:

7
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,200
did they eat, sleep, play?

8
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,600
Cats hide illness, so small changes

9
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:14,000
matter.

10
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,282
But here's the catch:

11
00:00:16,282 --> 00:00:18,176
last week, my camera decided this exercise

12
00:00:18,176 --> 00:00:18,988
ball was Qbo.

13
00:00:18,988 --> 00:00:19,800
For twenty-six minutes!

14
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,800
Why not send every frame to a big AI?

15
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:24,600
We tried:

16
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:27,800
eight minutes of video took an hour and

17
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,200
twenty-five dollars, and still missed a

18
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:30,600
cat.

19
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,600
A bigger model on the Pi?

20
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,200
It only runs YOLO nano, at three frames a

21
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:37,600
second:

22
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,000
almost free, but it makes mistakes.

23
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:44,000
A bigger detector is out of scope.

24
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,200
We keep the small model, and make it

25
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,400
smarter with AI.

26
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,000
So, we built both.

27
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,480
This is Agentic Realtime Computer Vision:

28
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:57,900
the AI gives the camera a brain, and the

29
00:00:57,900 --> 00:00:59,800
camera gives the AI eyes.

30
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,800
Here's how it works.

31
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,800
The Pi watches every frame.

32
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,600
When it's unsure, our bridge asks Meta's

33
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:09,000
Muse Spark, and remembers what's normal.

34
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,800
And doubts are rare:

35
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,400
twelve in eight minutes.

36
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,847
Each doubt has a name.

37
00:01:16,847 --> 00:01:18,494
There are fifteen kinds, like:

38
00:01:18,494 --> 00:01:20,800
I relabeled this cat by distance alone.

39
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,500
It becomes a plain-English question, with

40
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,800
evidence and a strict answer format.

41
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:28,835
Then the agent pulls the frames it needs,

42
00:01:28,835 --> 00:01:31,471
zooms into each cat, and answers with a

43
00:01:31,471 --> 00:01:31,800
reason.

44
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,200
Related doubts share a call:

45
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:36,200
twelve questions, just five calls.

46
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,600
Every verdict rewrites the record, and

47
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,200
every change is traceable.

48
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,236
Then there's memory.

49
00:01:43,236 --> 00:01:45,655
Not boxes and timestamps, but a diary:

50
00:01:45,655 --> 00:01:48,418
Qb slept in the green bed, from four

51
00:01:48,418 --> 00:01:49,800
thirty-four to four forty.

52
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:53,000
Over weeks, it learns what normal looks

53
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,800
like, for each cat, in each spot.

54
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,174
So, does it work?

55
00:01:57,174 --> 00:01:58,878
The tracker called the sleeping cat Qbo.

56
00:01:58,878 --> 00:02:00,826
The agent saw cool white fur and white

57
00:02:00,826 --> 00:02:01,070
paws:

58
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:01,557
that's Qb.

59
00:02:01,557 --> 00:02:01,800
Overturned!

60
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:04,767
Here, the tracker swapped two cats walking

61
00:02:04,767 --> 00:02:05,500
close together.

62
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,067
The agent checked both, and swapped them

63
00:02:08,067 --> 00:02:08,800
right back.

64
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,835
When the detector itself is wrong, the cat

65
00:02:11,835 --> 00:02:14,141
gets relabeled, and that ball becomes a

66
00:02:14,141 --> 00:02:14,800
known decoy.

67
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:17,400
Put together, the same eight minutes tell

68
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,343
the true story:

69
00:02:18,343 --> 00:02:21,171
Qb slept the whole time, and Qbo walked in

70
00:02:21,171 --> 00:02:21,800
and out.

71
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,000
The numbers?

72
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,200
One percent of frames call the AI, false

73
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:28,200
alarms drop ninety-three percent, and

74
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:31,000
ninety-nine percent of what the camera saw

75
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,600
gets the right cat.

76
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,200
All for thirty-nine cents!

77
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,600
And cats are just the start:

78
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:41,400
lab mice, tiny drones, cars in fog,

79
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,200
production lines.

80
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:45,000
Any small model watching for rare moments

81
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,200
has this gap.

82
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:47,600
Next:

83
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:50,400
run Muse Glimmer locally, give your own

84
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:53,200
agent these eyes, and let its verdicts

85
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,400
teach the Pi.

86
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:56,514
Agentic Realtime Computer Vision.

87
00:02:56,514 --> 00:02:58,814
Built this week, on Meta's Muse Spark.

88
00:02:58,814 --> 00:02:59,800
Thanks for watching!
